    "since": "2024",
    "bio_en": "Mauricio Pochettino is a high-profile managerial appointment designed to elevate the United States Men's National Team as they prepare to co-host the 2026 FIFA World Cup. Renowned for his high-energy, high-pressing tactical philosophy and his proven ability to develop world-class talent, Pochettino brings elite European experience from his time at clubs like Tottenham Hotspur, PSG, and Chelsea. His mission is to instill a world-class tactical identity and a winning mentality in a talented American generation. By demanding high physical standards and tactical discipline, he aims to lead the U.S. to their most successful World Cup campaign in history, inspiring a nation of fans during this landmark home tournament.",
